  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Why Won't My Under Cabinet Lights Turn On?",
    "text": "Why Won't My Under Cabinet Lights Turn On?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "It's super frustrating when you've just installed new under cabinet lights and they're not working! Often, it's a simple fix. First, always check the power source. Is it plugged in properly, or if hardwired, is the circuit breaker on? For LED strips, polarity is a huge one – make sure the positive and negative connections are correct. Even a tiny mismatch can stop them from lighting up. Weak or loose connections are another common culprit. Sometimes the adhesive isn't holding the strip firmly, or the connectors aren't fully seated. You'd be surprised how often a quick double-check of all connections solves the problem. And finally, if you're using a dimmer, make sure it's compatible with your specific lighting system. An incompatible dimmer can prevent your lights from turning on or cause them to flicker. If you've gone through all these and it's still dark, especially with hardwired systems, it might be time to call in someone like us at HH Remodeling LLC. We can quickly diagnose those trickier electrical issues and get your kitchen glowing again.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
